\title{Distributive monoid actions}
\author{brentyorgey}
\date{2026-01-10T00:02:58Z}
\taxon{Definition}

\p{In order for a [monoid action](003B) of #{S} on #{A} to be [distributive](0038), we additionally require it to satisfy the \em{annihilation law} ##{a \cdot e = e} for all #{a \in A}; if #{a \cdot -} is to be a monoid homomorphism then it must preserve the identity element.}
